WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.504
This is actually the
lead ship of Flight 19.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.605
Wow!

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.940
The exact same plane
as this is Flight 19.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.174
Yes.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.377
The final word to
the men on Flight 19

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.412
have been studied
and pored over.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:18.251
Every sentence and word
analyzed, in depth, by

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.588
the Navy's after action report.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.758
And then of course, re-analyzed
by armchair historians

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.293
and hacky curse TV shows.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.328
Walk me through it.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.929
What happened to Flight 19?

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.531
What's the deal?

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.134
TERRY RUSH: It was a training
flight for navigation training,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.668
believe it or not.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.238
So we just got back from
the Sapona, which we dove on.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.639
That was their target.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.241
So we know they dropped
their bombs on the Sapona.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.308
TERRY RUSH: Correct.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.276
What was their
path after that?

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.110
TERRY RUSH: Due east.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.078
Due east.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.813
For another 60, 70 miles.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.114
OK.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.083
Then make a turn to
the north, northwest.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.217
What happened?

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.652
It's a big
mystery to this day.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.787
Right.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.321
Nobody knows exactly
what happened to them.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.757
Nobody knows, but
there are theories.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:01.828
Colleen Sterling is the LeBron
James of aviation probability

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.363
analysis.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.198
You maybe didn't know there
was a LeBron James of that.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.768
After two years of searching
for Air France Flight 447,

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.271
Colleen was brought in
as part of a small team

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.139
to reanalyze the data.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.309
They found the wreckage
in less than five days.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.877
COLLEEN STERLING:
The first thing

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:21.848
we did is looked at the 500
page Navy report that came out.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:25.185
The communications, all the
radar hits that they had,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.920
and we wrote a chronology.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:30.023
The key transmissions,
everything is map based, right?

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.624
Right.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.826
COLLEEN STERLING: So I'll put
like where they launched from

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.394
and the time.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.429
And then I'll draw the line
where they were supposed to go.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.365
And then I can calculate with
the wind and their heading,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.700
how long it should
have taken them to get

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.435
to their first turn point.
- Uh-huh.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.204
COLLEEN STERLING: I thought
about that first turn point

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.305
and then I said,
well, where could

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.639
they have gone from there?

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:49.142
They were trying to go
back to the northwest,

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.544
but the wind was blowing
them and they may have not

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.280
made the turn sharp enough and
might have got significantly

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.683
blown to a different heading.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.451
Powers.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.753
What is your compass
reading, Powers?

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.355
I don't know where we are.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.524
Must have gotten lost
after that last turn.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:08.328
NT-28, this is FT-74,
what is your trouble?

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.397
Oh, both my compasses are
out and I'm trying to find

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.066
Fort Lauderdale, Florida.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.634
So this is the compass here.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.102
TERRY RUSH: That's
the magnetic compass.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.670
That's the magnetic compass.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.372
So he would be looking at this.
What else would he look at?

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.107
TERRY RUSH: He would look
at that and then he'd-- down

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.076
on his instrument panel,
you have what's called

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.511
the gyrocompass here.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.313
That you set this with this
knob to agree with this.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.348
To agree with-- to that.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.482
TERRY RUSH: This bounces around.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.450
Sure.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.851
TERRY RUSH: That
one is very stable.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.453
COLLEEN STERLING: Taylor,
who's the flight lead,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.955
was talking about the
compass didn't look right.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.156
He started to get confused.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.491
Don't they know
they have to get back?

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.193
COLLEEN STERLING: Taylor
thought that they needed

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.795
to fly to the northeast
because he thought they

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.297
were over the Florida Keys.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.632
How did you think--

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.200
COLLEEN STERLING: It's
very hard to imagine

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.735
him getting that lost.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.205
He didn't seem to have his
wits about him on this flight.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.240
Then you hear them
arguing on the radio.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.408
It's really sad.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.442
But--

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.344
We've just passed
over a small island

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.280
and we have no
other land in sight.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.715
Turn on your
emergency IFF gear.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.150
Or do you have it on?

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.285
IFF gear was off.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.686
I'm turning it on now.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.187
What's IFF gear?

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.924
TERRY RUSH: IFF, that's an
acronym for Identification,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.858
Friend or Foe.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.426
OK.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.028
TERRY RUSH: Right here, for
example, see this says 1,200.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.897
And then IFF, they would have
given him a code to squawk.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.098
To put as friend.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.099
TERRY RUSH: Put in
there and it would

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.601
be picked up on their radar.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.302
He didn't have it on.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.336
He didn't have it on.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.804
Should he have had it on?

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.940
Especially if I want help
in finding out where I am.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.341
Right.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.444
FT-28 to [inaudible]
[inaudible] 3,

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.815
one of the planes in the flight
thinks if we went 270 degrees,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.250
we could hit land.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:38.785
TERRY RUSH: 270,
that's due west.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.187
Somebody with a decent compass
or somebody else is like,

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.322
hey we just go 270.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.656
We're going to hit
land eventually.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.891
TERRY RUSH: To get to
their bombing target,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.492
they flew due east.
- Right.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.227
TERRY RUSH: Well just fly due
west and it'd take you back--

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.395
[interposing voices]

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.163
TERRY RUSH: --where
you came from.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.130
Yeah, right.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:51.965
We'll hit land some point.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.166
TERRY RUSH: Yeah.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.334
FT-28 all planes
in flight, change

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.704
course to 0 90 for 1 minute.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.738
So now they're going--

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.139
TERRY RUSH: Back east again.
- Powers.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.374
Back east again.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.843
And if we just fly
west, we would get home.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.811
Hold it.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.179
Head west.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.780
[inaudible]

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:10.883
COLLEEN STERLING: Powers, who is
the ranking guy on the flight,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.985
he kept saying we
need to go west.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.119
Right.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.687
COLLEEN STERLING:
And then it gets

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.757
corroborated with a radar track
that came from the Solomons

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:18.791
aircraft carrier.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:19.892
And where did that see them?

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.994
COLLEEN STERLING:
The radar track

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.329
showed aircraft going south.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.130
Huh.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.465
COLLEEN STERLING: Over land.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.066
There's a good
chance that it could

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.736
be somewhere in this
mid-peninsula, east coast

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:30.970
of Florida region.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.138
So that wouldn't
surprise you at all.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.072
COLLEEN STERLING: No.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.340
The model supports that.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.174
Wow.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.111
We are now flying 270 degrees.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.980
We will fly 270 degrees
until we hit the beach

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.548
or run out of gas.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.417
[dramatic music]

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.386
And now they know they're
in trouble because it's like--

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.520
TERRY RUSH: They're out of time.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.955
They're going
to run out of gas.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.289
TERRY RUSH: Yeah.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.624
And they just don't have
a clue where they are.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.060
When the first plane
drops below 10 gallons,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.162
we all go down together.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.263
Everyone understand that?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.331
[dramatic music]

